  ;; lease :unknown, not :known across a window never observed.\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:897:      (is (= :unknown (get-in system [:judge :ledger :l1 :evidence]))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:924:        (is (= :unknown (get-in system [:judge :ledger :l1 :evidence]))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:925:            \"the gapped medium's lease is unknown\")\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:949:      (is (= :unknown (get-in system [:judge :ledger :l1 :evidence])))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:956:    ;; duration -- the contract's Limits tolerance, not a contradiction of\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:979:  (testing \"J9: a tick-cursor gap makes the pass late, not the leases unknown\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:993:          \"a tick gap marks nothing unknown\")\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1165:          \"no answer is owed and none was authored\"))))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1524:    ;; the lease unknown with a fresh resumed reading -- repeat forever and\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1593:                       :resolver (fn [source _] source)\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1607:          ;; a grant in a foreign unit enters the queue via the one-arg gate\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1679:  (testing \"N1: a reading far past 10^6 magnitudes is legal and ordered\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1713:          \"the largest legal :s magnitude against an ms-based table\"))))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1717:  (testing \"N1: a table magnitude past 2^52 is refused at assembly\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1721:                             :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)})))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1724:                             :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)})))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1726:                                     :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)}))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1814:(deftest r3-tolerance-validated-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1815:  (testing \"N4: a tolerance in a foreign unit is refused at assembly\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1817:      (is (= :tolerance\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1819:                               :tolerance bad\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1820:                               :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)})))))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1821:  (testing \"N4/R3: the tolerance bound is per-unit, not raw\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1822:    (is (= :tolerance\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1824:                             :tolerance {:s 4503599627370496}\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1825:                             :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)}))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1827:  (testing \"legal tolerances assemble\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1829:                                     :tolerance {:ms 0}\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1830:                                     :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)})))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1832:                                     :tolerance nil\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1833:                                     :resolver (fn [_source _fact] nil)})))))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1836:(deftest r3-resolver-throw-drops-element-and-continues-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1837:  (testing \"N5: a resolver throwing on a hostile envelope drops that element\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1838:    (let [resolver (fn [_source fact]\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1843:                     (update :judge assoc :resolver resolver)\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1864:(deftest r4-judge-without-a-resolver-throws-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1865:  (testing \"R1: a missing resolver is an assembly defect, not dropped facts\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1868:        \"a judge assembled with no resolver must throw before any step,\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1871:                 (lease/initial-judge {:resolver :not-a-fn})))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1872:    (is (some? (lease/initial-judge {:resolver (fn [_source _fact] :x)}))))\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1873:  (testing \"R1: a constructed judge whose facts arrive never lapses via drops\"\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:5:# Task: confirm the R1–R4 fixes — final gate for dao.lease Phase 1+2\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:9:Your R1–R4 findings were fixed. Provenance note: the implementer's fixes\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:12:`initial-judge`, and `:resolver` added to five pre-existing assembly-test\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:13:configs your R1 gate had started to trip) and re-verified the full matrix:\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:19:- R1: `initial-judge` throws at assembly unless `:resolver` is a function,\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:20:  with the rationale comment; new test `r4-judge-without-a-resolver-throws-test`\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:21:  (plus `:resolver :not-a-fn` refusal and a valid-resolver success case).\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:22:- R2: `:abort-error` starts nil in `initial-judge` and `judge-step` resets\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:24:- R3: tolerance validated for shape, unit membership, AND the per-unit\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:26:- R4: `drain-ticks` docstring states the actual two behaviors, and the new\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:28:- R5: recorded as a Phase 4 design note in the plan's §6 (no code change).\ncollab/1789840100000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:30:Re-read only the lines R1–R4 touched and the r4 test. Challenge the fixes.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:8:accepted; P3-unknown-tolerance is a contract-owner question; P3 misconfig\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:39:- Overflowing that medium produces a gap, which marks L `unknown` with `:resumed = now` (818-833).\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:40:- Repeating this faster than one duration means L is never reclaimed for silence. This is delegated renewal in effect, and it defeats the per-attachment isolation the contract's Limits section relies on.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:51:  - Bound magnitudes in `duration?`, or use `*'` under `:clj`.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:54:**P1 | lease.cljc:515, 772 against plan D4 and finding 9 | The resolver is called as `(resolver fact)`, not `(resolver source fact)`.**\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:58:- Fix: have `wire-facts` take a source, and call `((:resolver judge) (:source entry) fact)`.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:84:**P2 | lease.cljc:818-833, 858-860 | A lease is not marked `unknown` when its medium gaps before any of its facts were observed there.**\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:96:- Fix at least the attacker-driven growth described in the first P1. Note the rest as owed.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:107:- The `unknown` silence bound leaves out tolerance.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:108:- With tolerance 5 and duration 10, a lease last observed at 100 that gaps at 101 becomes due after 111. Without the gap it would be due after 115.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:111:**P3 | lease.cljc:237-296 | The structural gate leaves gaps.**\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:119:- `interval` and `add-duration` throw mid-pass on an incommensurate unit table or a tolerance in a foreign unit.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:120:- An `unknown` entry with no `:resumed` reading throws a null-pointer error at 1011. A recovered persisted ledger is the case the contract names, and no recovery helper exists.\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:121:- These can be deferred to `make-judge`, but they should be listed as owed.\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:35:  `apply-tick-value` against its own stream), bound magnitudes so no host\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:40:- P1-5 resolver: `wire-facts`/`wire-tick` take a source; the judge calls\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:41:  `(resolver source fact)` per revised-plan D4. Grantor-authored facts keep\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:52:  first renewal → medium gap must leave the lease `:unknown`. Choose the\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:53:  mechanism (grant-declared medium, or conservative unknown-marking) and\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:60:  legitimate-use growth as owed to the persistence design (do not build\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:66:- P3 structural gate: shape-check `:dao.lease/duration`, `:dao.lease/max`\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:71:  `:drain-budget`, validates unit-table commensurability, and an `unknown`\ncollab/1789833230000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:78:- P3 unknown-silence tolerance: NO code change — the code matches the\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:10:**N1 (P1, regression from the P1-4 fix) | `lease.cljc:39-46, 59-71, 760-766` | The 10⁶ magnitude bound gives the judge a finite lifetime, and it ends silently.**\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:11:- `duration?` also gates `:dao.lease/reading`, and readings never decrease. A millisecond tick stream therefore becomes structurally defective after 1000 seconds. A second-resolution stream lasts about 11.6 days.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:17:  - Bound the base product, not the raw magnitude: in `duration?`, require n ≤ 2^52.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:18:  - When a unit table is supplied, also require `n ≤ (quot 2^52 unit-magnitude)` as a structural defect. That check divides, so it cannot overflow.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:34:- If the holder's own medium truncates or gaps before its first renewal is observed, the lease is neither suppressed (`silence-suppressed`, 1168-1171) nor marked unknown (`mark-medium-unknown`, 956-957). That is a false lapse over a window the judge never observed.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:38:**N4 (P2, new) | `lease.cljc:622, 1140-1142` | `:tolerance` is never validated.**\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:39:- `tolerance?` is defined at line 74 and never called.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:40:- A tolerance in a unit outside the table throws from `add-duration` inside `classify-entry`. Step 4 has no try/catch, so the throw escapes `judge-step` after step 3 has already appended grants.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:43:- Remaining action: in `initial-judge`, check `tolerance?`, check that its unit is in the table, and add the test.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:46:- The catch returns the judge and cursor entry as they were before the drain. An exception raised while processing a value, such as a resolver that throws on a hostile envelope, therefore re-reads the same element every pass. Reclamation halts for every lease.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:53:  - Catch `Exception` on clj and store the message under an `:abort-error` key.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:56:- This includes an attacker's own per-author medium. A truncated medium suppresses `:silence` for every never-renewed lease, and a gapped one re-marks them `unknown` with a fresh resumed reading.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:58:- Remaining action: record it in §6 as owed to \"the grant declares its medium\" in Phase 4.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:68:| P1-5 resolver bound to source | **Fixed** | 742-751, `wire-facts` source, test 643 | none |\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:75:| P2-7 `:seen`/`:answered` growth | **Accepted as owed** | attacker-driven paths closed; legitimate growth documented at 607-611 | none |\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:77:| P3 unknown-state tolerance | **Routed to contract owner** | §6 | none |\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:79:| P3 assembly validation | **Partly fixed** | budget and units validated at 615-620; tolerance is not | see N4 |\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:6:**Not ready to commit: one blocker remains, R1.** N1–N4 are confirmed fixed. N5 is fixed as prescribed, but the fix silently swallows a missing resolver (R1 below). I edited nothing and did not rerun suites.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:10:| N1 magnitude bound | **Fixed** | `magnitude-limit` is 2⁵² (`lease.cljc:39-50`); the per-unit check uses division, so it cannot overflow (`base-over-bound`, 261-274, applied 290-292). Products stay ≤ 2⁵² and sums ≤ 2⁵³, exact on all three hosts. A defective tick on a tick cursor is now counted (807-808). Tests at 1662-1727. | Optional, see R3. |\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:13:| N4 tolerance not validated | **Fixed** | `initial-judge` checks `tolerance?` and that the unit is in the table (655-661). Test at 1795. | Optional, see R3. |\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:14:| N5 silent permanent abort | **Fixed, but introduces R1** | A throw while processing a value drops it, advances the cursor and continues (1087-1100). A throw from the read aborts with `:abort-error` (884-888, 1145-1148). Catches take `Exception` under `:clj`. Test at 1807. | R1 (required); R2 and R4 are minor. |\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:18:**R1 (P2, regression from the N5 fix; fix before commit) | `lease.cljc:785-794, 1088-1093` | A missing resolver is now swallowed silently.**\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:19:- `resolve-author` throws when `:resolver` is nil, and that throw happens inside the new per-element `try`.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:20:- A judge assembled without a resolver now drops every lease fact as `:element-threw`. `initial-judge` does not check for one, and its docstring defers that check to a constructor that does not exist yet.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:23:  - In `initial-judge`, or at the top of `judge-step`, outside the `try`, throw when `:resolver` is not a function.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:24:  - Add a test that a judge with no resolver throws and does not lapse its leases.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:26:**R2 (P3) | `lease.cljc:1434` | `:abort-error` is never cleared.**\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:27:- `judge-step` resets `:abort` but leaves `:abort-error`, so an old message persists into later healthy passes. The key is also missing from the `initial-judge` map.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:28:- Remaining action: `(assoc judge :abort nil :abort-error nil)`.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:30:**R3 (P3) | `lease.cljc:655-661` | Tolerance gets the raw bound but not the per-unit bound.**\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:31:- A tolerance of `{:h 4503599627370496}` passes assembly, then overflows a long in `add-duration` mid-pass on the JVM.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:33:- Remaining action: apply the same `quot` check to the tolerance at assembly.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:35:**R4 (P3) | `lease.cljc:838, 873-875` | The tick path does not match its docstring.**\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:40:**R5 (P3, design note; no change needed for this commit) | A renewal dropped because the resolver threw still counts against the holder.**\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:41:- A transient resolver failure on a genuine renewal can therefore become a false lapse.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:17:- N1: `magnitude-limit` 2⁵² raw bound in `duration?`/`tolerance?`; the\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:18:  division-based per-unit check `n > (quot 2⁵² unit-magnitude)` joined the\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:19:  universal shape gate; table magnitudes bounded at assembly; a defective\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:26:  is the delivery gate). Two-holder same-pid test added.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:29:- N4: `initial-judge` validates `:tolerance` shape and unit membership.\ncollab/1789839800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:31:  continue); read throws still abort with `:abort-error`; catches take\ncollab/1789841143000-architect-dao-lease-p12-signoff.prompt.md:13:(N1: magnitude bound aged out tick streams; R1: missing-resolver swallow);\ncollab/1789841143000-architect-dao-lease-p12-signoff.prompt.md:14:and a final reviewer gate (source clean; a test-only T1 gate, applied and\ncollab/1789841143000-architect-dao-lease-p12-signoff.prompt.md:36:3. Is anything owed-but-undocumented (the plan's §6 must be an honest\ncollab/1789841143000-architect-dao-lease-p12-signoff.prompt.md:39:You are NOT asked to relitigate closed findings or to hunt new nits — the\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.prompt.md:46:3. Incomplete evidence: gap→unknown marking per medium, the `:resumed` silence\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.prompt.md:49:4. The vocabulary gate: `defective?` (structural, V4) vs `admissible?`\ncollab/1789832533000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12.prompt.md:51:   gate or vice versa, and do the constructors reject everything the contract\ncollab/1789835563000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:21:  reviewer's scheme: raw magnitudes bounded at 2⁵² (`duration?`/`tolerance?`\ncollab/1789835563000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:22:  — tolerance permitting zero), and against a supplied unit table also\ncollab/1789835563000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:23:  `n ≤ (quot 2⁵² unit-magnitude)` — division-based, so overflow-free. Then\ncollab/1789835563000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:42:- **N4 (P2):** `initial-judge` validates `:tolerance` — `tolerance?` shape\ncollab/1789835563000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:46:  continues (store the message under an `:abort-error` key only for real\ncollab/1789835563000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r3.prompt.md:51:  two behaviors. Test: a resolver that throws on a hostile envelope — the\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:10:(this tree's copy), section \"Remaining defects\", R1–R4.\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:13:Failing test first for R1.\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:17:- **R1 (P2, blocker):** a judge assembled without a `:resolver` must throw —\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:19:  throw unless `:resolver` is a function. Add the test: a judge with no\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:20:  resolver throws at assembly (or on its first step, outside any catch), and\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:23:- **R2 (P3):** `judge-step` resets both — `(assoc judge :abort nil\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:24:  :abort-error nil)` — and `:abort-error` starts nil in the\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:26:- **R3 (P3):** apply the same per-unit `quot` bound to `:tolerance` at\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:28:- **R4 (P3):** fix the `drain-ticks` docstring to match the code (or wrap\ncollab/1789837726000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p12-r4.prompt.md:32:- **R5:** no code change — Phase 4 design note; the orchestrator has it.\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:15:code; the plan gained a J16 suppression amendment (D7), and §6 gained owed rows\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:21:  while-truncated; authoritative-only medium registration; magnitude bound\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:23:  throws into abort; resolver bound to source).\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:27:  unknown-marking for the gap-before-first-renewal case, documented;\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:29:  attacker growth gone via P1-1/P1-3, legitimate growth documented as owed;\ncollab/1789833800000-reviewer-dao-lease-p12-r2.prompt.md:33:  the direct proof; unknown-tolerance question routed to the contract owner\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
