{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1848,1895p' test/dao/lease_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"                     (fact! (lease/renewal :l1))\n                     (tick! 7)\n                     step!)]\n      (is (= 1 (get-in system [:judge :dropped]))\n          \"the poisoned element was dropped\")\n      (is (= {:ms 7} (get-in system [:judge :ledger :l1 :last-observation]))\n          \"the cursor advanced past it and the clean renewal after it was\n           applied: judging continues\")\n      (is (nil? (get-in system [:judge :abort]))\n          \"a processing throw is not a transport abort\"))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; r4 review findings\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest r4-judge-without-a-resolver-throws-test\n  (testing \"R1: a missing resolver is an assembly defect, not dropped facts\"\n    (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n                 (lease/initial-judge {}))\n        \"a judge assembled with no resolver must throw before any step,\n         never silently drop every lease fact into :dropped\")\n    (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n                 (lease/initial-judge {:resolver :not-a-fn})))\n    (is (some? (lease/initial-judge {:resolver (fn [_source _fact] :x)}))))\n  (testing \"R1: a constructed judge whose facts arrive never lapses via drops\"\n    (let [log (atom [])\n          system (-> (setup {:reclaim (fn [subject] (swap! log conj subject) true)})\n                     grant!\n                     (tick! 1)\n                     step!\n                     (tick! 7)\n                     (renewal-from :l1 :holder-a)\n                     step!\n                     (tick! 15)\n                     step!)]\n      (is (= 0 (get-in system [:judge :dropped]))\n          \"every fact that arrived was read and applied\")\n      (is (= [] @log)\n          \"the renewal counted: no false :silence over an observed holder\")\n      (is (contains? (get-in system [:judge :ledger]) :l1)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"The Phase 1+2 code is architecturally sound, but commit sign-off is blocked by an inaccurate implementation-plan boundary.\n\n- Attribution and authority: pass. Attribution is source-bound through `(resolver source fact)`; only grantor-authored facts establish terms; only holder-authored renewals and releases affect a lease.\n- Conservative evidence: pass. Gaps produce `unknown`; truncated fact drains suppress silence; malformed or failed reads cannot manufacture absence evidence.\n- Record-after-act: pass. Reclaim state becomes `pending` before the reclaim operation, and `:lapsed` is written only after reported success.\n- Architectural surface: pass. `dao.lease` depends only on `dao.stream`, reads no host clock, and owns no scheduler, callback, registry, or mutable global state.\n- Reconciliation fixes: consistent. The N1 magnitude correction and R1–R4 corrections agree with their docstrings and surrounding behavior.\n\nThe blocker is [dao.lease.implementation-plan.md](/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-lease/docs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:521): the host matrix and §6 claim that the holder, `make-judge`/`make-holder`, composition constructors, tests, and use-case sketches are already built. They are not present; [dao.lease.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-lease/src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:9) correctly says they will join later. Phase 3 and Phase 4 must therefore be listed as owing, not built. Additionally, §6 omits R5—the documented Phase 4 obligation to address transient resolver failures conservatively—even though the final-gate brief says it was recorded.\n\nNo source change is required for Phase 1+2; the plan must be corrected so §6 honestly describes the delivered boundary.\n\nSIGN-OFF: denied — the Phase 1+2 implementation honors the contract, but the plan falsely marks unimplemented Phase 3+4 work as built and omits the R5 obligation."}}
